# PART I — Maven

**1.a)** Clone using `git clone https://github.com/deepthisagar7/library-management.git`, then import the project in Eclipse using **File → Import → Maven → Existing Maven Projects → select project → Finish**.

**1.b)** Set `<packaging>jar</packaging>`, Java source/target to `17`, and configure the `maven-compiler-plugin` for Java 17 in `pom.xml`.

**1.c)** `clean` deletes previous build files, `compile` compiles source code, `test` runs tests, `package` creates the JAR, and `install` stores the JAR in the local Maven repository; **`package` generates the JAR**.

**1.d)** Run `mvn clean package`.

**1.e)** Run `java -version` and `mvn -version`, ensure Maven uses JDK 17, set `JAVA_HOME` to JDK 17 if required, and rerun `mvn clean package`.

**1.f)** Check for a missing `Main-Class`, incorrect Java version, or missing dependencies by checking the manifest/JAR, running `java -version`, and using `mvn dependency:tree`.

**1.g)** Compare `java -version` and `mvn -version`, configure Maven compiler/enforcer settings to require Java 17, and use the same JDK version across development and deployment to avoid compatibility problems.

