# PART III — Docker

**3.a)** Create a `Dockerfile` using `FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jre`, `WORKDIR /app`, `COPY target/library-management.jar app.jar`, `EXPOSE 8080`, and `CMD ["java","-jar","app.jar"]`.

**3.b)** Build using `docker build -t library-management:latest .` and run using `docker run -d -p 8080:8080 --name library-management-container library-management:latest`.

**3.c)** Check `docker ps`, `docker ps -a`, `docker logs library-management-container`, and `docker port library-management-container` to verify the container, application, and port mapping.

**3.d)** A 404 usually means the requested URL/endpoint is incorrect or the application has a context path; verify the correct endpoint and check application execution using `docker logs <container>` and `docker exec -it <container> sh`.
